  "coverage": "complete",
  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 7 actions (src/actions.ts) and 4 feedbacks (src/feedbacks.ts: 2 boolean, 2 advanced), each registered in a single call.",
    "sACN (E1.31) over UDP, default port 5568 (src/constants.ts); the module can transmit, receive, or both, one universe per connection. Config (not in the schema): universe (1-63999, default 1), localAddress, mode (none, send, receive), enableSender, enableReceiver, source name, UUID, priority (1-201, default 100), custom target IP, slow update interval (default 800 ms, 10-10000) and fast interval (default 40 ms, 5-1000) in src/config.ts.",
    "Every numeric field of the actions is a textinput with useVariables, so values are strings that the callbacks convert with Number() after resolving variables. Nothing in the module range-checks channel numbers or values in the options; the callbacks pass them to the transitions code, which is not catalogued.",
    "fadeValues and offset_multiple use regex /((^| )([1-9]?[0-9]|1[0-9]{2}|2[0-4][0-9]|25[0-5])){1,512}$/ (recorded as written). The regex has no start anchor and only allows spaces between numbers, although the label and the callback (valuesRaw.replaceAll(':', ' ')) also accept colons. The offset_multiple values are described as change values but the regex allows only 0-255 (no minus sign).",
    "The feedback 'value' options of chan_matches_value and chan_greater_than are textinputs without useVariables (src/feedbacks.ts:22, 53); the callbacks compare Number(value) with Number(self.data[channel - 1]). chan_rgb with 16-Bit reads only the high bytes (channels c, c+2, c+4).",
    "16-bit actions (setValue16, offset_single_16, percent_single_flex with resolution) address the MSB on the given channel and the LSB on the next one. percent_single_flex converts percent to 0-255 or 0-65535 and adds the current value when 'Use offset' is set.",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~1.12.1: options do not support expressions."
  ],
